DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_1 = Formula("x+1");
$fun_2 = Formula("ln(x)");
$fun_3 = Formula("(cos(x))/8");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>9)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>7)}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>1)}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>9)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_3]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_3->D()}
- [`f'(8) =`] [_____]{$fun_3->D()->eval(x=>8)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
